WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.200
- [Narrator] In the
Indian city of Amritsar,

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.700
there is a shining temple

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.528
that is one of the most
visited places in the world.

00:00:07.528 --> 00:00:10.195
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:15.580
The Harmandir Sahibor,
or the Golden Temple,

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.720
is the chief house of worship
for the Sikh religion.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.120
The name literally
translates to "House of God".

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.310
And millions of Sikhs travel to the temple

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.893
every month on pilgrimage.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.250
Surrounded by a pool of holy water,

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.930
the temple was founded in 1574

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:34.380
to be a place of worship for men and women

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.693
of all walks of life to worship equally.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.290
The temple was constructed
out of marble and copper

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:43.580
and is covered with a layer of gold foil,

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.773
giving the temple its signature shine.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.130
Perhaps the most impressive
part of the temple

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.803
is the langar, the Sikh community kitchen.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:57.570
Every day they provide more
than 100,000 free meals

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.893
in one of the largest
kitchens in the world.

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:04.290
No matter a visitor's reason
for going to the Golden Temple,

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:05.650
they will surely be impressed

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:08.491
by the architecture,
history and community.

00:01:08.491 --> 00:01:12.158
(dramatic orchestral music)

